1z1o|v|To press between two bodies; to press together closely; to compress; often, to compress so as to expel juice, moisture, etc.; as, to squeeze an orange with the fingers; to squeeze the hand in friendship. ; Fig.: To oppress with hardships, burdens, or taxes; to harass; to crush. ; To force, or cause to pass, by compression; often with out, through, etc.; as, to squeeze water through felt. ; To press; to urge one's way, or to pass, by pressing; to crowd; -- often with through, into, etc.; as, to squeeze hard to get through a crowd.	D:1g31,13,1~1g31,13,1
